@fm description | description | Notes for the Crumbwick Bakery crew about shifts, breaks and how to ask for help.
# Staff notes
s description | The crew has eleven people and three shifts: opening, middle and closing.
s none | Welcome to Crumbwick.
## Shifts
t none | Shift | none | Starts | none | Ends
t description | Opening | description | Half past five | description | Half past one
t description | Middle | description | Nine | description | Five
t description | Closing | description | Noon | description | Half past six
s rule{staff_late} | Phone the shop manager at least one hour before the shift if you will be late.
s prohibition | Do not swap a shift without the shop manager's written note.
s gate{staff_swap} | Write the swap in the shift book before you tell the other person.
## Breaks
l rule | Take your break away from the ovens and the loft
l gate | Wash your hands before you return to the shelves
l prohibition{staff_floor} | Do not eat on the shop floor
l description | The break room is the small room at the end of the back corridor
l example | A crew member who ate a roll behind the till left crumbs that a customer later complained about
## Uniform
s rule | Wear the white apron and the grey cap in the loft and at the ovens.
s prohibition | Do not wear rings in the loft.
s description | Aprons are washed on Sunday by the closing crew.
s example | Case: a ring dropped into a trough once and the whole batch of dough had to be searched.
## Asking for help
s rule{staff_help} | Ask the head baker if you do not know a step.
s rule | Write a question in the question book if the head baker is away.
s gate | Read the question book at the start of each shift.
s description | The question book lies on the table in the break room.
s none | Nobody minds a good question.
